The library provides methods for addition, subtraction, multiplication, division, modulus calculation, degree expansion, and root extraction for complex numbers. The implementation uses constructors to create complex numbers, getters and setters to access the class fields, and friend functions for arithmetic operations and other mathematical operations on complex numbers.

The library also includes static methods and variables. The static method "calculateModulus" calculates the modulus of a complex number, and the static variable "counter" can be used to keep count of the number of instances of the Complex class.

