`SDL_RenderCopyEx()` is used to render a portion of a source texture onto the rendering target (either the screen or a custom render target) with rotation and flip options. It does not work directly with render textures.

To draw a different texture onto the render texture, you would need to create a new render texture and copy the contents of the original render texture, along with the additional texture, using `SDL_RenderCopy()` or `SDL_RenderCopyEx()` to the new render texture.

