```csharp
public class HideRefererAttribute : ActionFilterAttribute
{
    public override void OnActionExecuted(ActionExecutedContext filterContext)
    {
        filterContext.HttpContext.Request.Headers["Referer"] = null;
        base.OnActionExecuted(filterContext);
    }
}
```

2. Apply the `HideRefererAttribute` to the specific action or controller where you want to hide the referer header. For example:

```csharp
[HideReferer]
public ActionResult SecurePage()
{
    // Your action code here
    return View();
}
```

3. In the `OnActionExecuted` method of the `HideRefererAttribute`, set the `Referer` header value to null, effectively hiding it from the request headers.

This approach will modify the `Referer` header value only for the specific actions or controllers decorated with the `HideRefererAttribute`.

