Instead of directly fetching entities, you can use DTO (Data Transfer Object) projection to retrieve specific data. This allows you to fetch only the required properties instead of the entire entity graph. By doing so, you can avoid LazyInitializationExceptions. Here's an example of how to use DTO projection:

```java
public List<A> loadAllDataWithListProperty() {
    try (Session session = HibernateUtil.getSessionFactory().openSession()) {
        CriteriaBuilder builder = session.getCriteriaBuilder();
        CriteriaQuery<A> criteria = builder.createQuery(A.class);
        Root<A> root = criteria.from(A.class);

        // Fetch the required properties using DTO projection
        criteria.select(builder.construct(A.class, root.get("id"), root.get("listProperty")));

        return session.createQuery(criteria).getResultList();
    }
}
```

By explicitly selecting the required properties in the query, Hibernate will fetch them directly, avoiding the LazyInitializationException.

