The `main()` function is the entry point of a Rust program, which is where execution will start when the program is run. Every Rust executable program must have a `main()` function.

To fix this error, make sure you have a `main()` function defined in your code. It should have the following signature:

```rust
fn main() {
    // Code goes here
}
```

Any code that you want to be executed when running the program should be placed inside the `main()` function.

