Apologies for the confusion. The issue you described occurs because the code checks if the text at the current caret position is empty or only contains whitespace before inserting a highlighted line. When you press Enter without any whitespace in the line, the code considers the line as empty and does not create the highlighted line.

To fix this issue and ensure that the highlighted line is inserted correctly, you can modify the insertLine() function as follows:

```javascript
function insertLine() {
  const range = window.getSelection().getRangeAt(0);
  if (range.startContainer.nodeType === 3) {
    const textNode = range.startContainer;
    const currentPosition = range.startOffset;
    const lineText = textNode.textContent.trim().slice(0, currentPosition);
    if (lineText === '') return;
    const highlightedLine = document.createElement('span');
    highlightedLine.classList.add('highlight-line');
    highlightedLine.textContent = '█';
    range.deleteContents();
    range.insertNode(highlightedLine);
    range.collapse();
    setTimeout(() => {
      highlightedLine.remove();
    }, 500);
  }
}
```

By using the `trim()` method to remove leading and trailing whitespace characters, the code now considers a line as non-empty as long as it contains at least one visible character. This ensures that the highlighted line will be inserted correctly when you press Enter.

