Here is the Java code to implement a stack ADT using two queues:

```java
class S {
    Queue<Integer> Q_1; // one queue instance
    Queue<Integer> Q_2; // another queue instance

    // Constructor
    public S() {
        Q_1 = new LinkedList<>();
        Q_2 = new LinkedList<>();
    }

    // Function to remove the top element from the stack
    public int pop() {
        if (isEmpty()) {
            throw new NoSuchElementException("Stack is empty");
        }

        // Move all elements from Q_1 to Q_2 except the last element
        while (Q_1.size() > 1) {
            Q_2.add(Q_1.remove());
        }

        // Remove the last element from Q_1 (which is our top element)
        int topElement = Q_1.remove();

        // Swap the names of Q_1 and Q_2
        Queue<Integer> temp = Q_1;
        Q_1 = Q_2;
        Q_2 = temp;

        return topElement;
    }

    // Function to add an element to the top of the stack
    public void push(int x) {
        // Enqueue the new element to Q_1
        Q_1.add(x);
    }

    // Function to check if the stack is empty
    public boolean isEmpty() {
        return Q_1.isEmpty();
    }

