To set the perspective mode when rendering a spinning cube in Forge 1.12.2 drawScreen, you can follow these steps:

1. Create a new class that extends GuiScreen. This will be your custom screen where you'll render your spinning cube.

```java
public class MyScreen extends GuiScreen {

    private static final int CUBE_SIZE = 50;
    private float rotation;

    @Override
    public void drawScreen(int mouseX, int mouseY, float partialTicks) {
        // Set the perspective mode
        GlStateManager.matrixMode(GL11.GL_PROJECTION);
        GlStateManager.loadIdentity();
        // Set the perspective view (with the desired settings)
        GLU.gluPerspective(45.0F, this.width / this.height, 0.1F, 100.0F);
        GlStateManager.matrixMode(GL11.GL_MODELVIEW);
        GlStateManager.loadIdentity();

        // Translate to the center of the screen
        GlStateManager.translate(this.width / 2, this.height / 2, 0);

        // Rotate the cube
        GlStateManager.rotate(rotation, 1, 1, 1);
        rotation += partialTicks;

        // Render your cube here (using vertices or VBOs)

        super.drawScreen(mouseX, mouseY, partialTicks);
    }

    // Other methods (e.g., initGui, mouseClicked) can be implemented as needed
}
```

