3. Define the `renderCube` method to handle the rendering of the spinning cube:

```java
public void renderCube(float partialTicks) {
    int size = 100; // Adjust the size of the cube as necessary

    // Set up OpenGL to enable 3D rendering and perspective mode
    GL11.glPushMatrix();
    GL11.glMatrixMode(GL11.GL_PROJECTION);
    GL11.glLoadIdentity();
    GL11.glOrtho(0, event.getResolution().getScaledWidth(), event.getResolution().getScaledHeight(), 0, 1, -1);
    GL11.glMatrixMode(GL11.GL_MODELVIEW);
    GL11.glLoadIdentity();
    GL11.glDisable(GL11.GL_DEPTH_TEST);

    // Translate and rotate the cube for spinning effect
    GL11.glTranslatef(event.getResolution().getScaledWidth() / 2, event.getResolution().getScaledHeight() / 2, 0);
    GL11.glRotatef(partialTicks * 50, 1, 1, 1);

    // Set cube color
    GL11.glColor3f(1.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f); // Red color

    // Render cube
    GL11.glBegin(GL11.GL_QUADS);
    GL11.glVertex3f(-size, -size, -size);
    GL11.glVertex3f(size, -size, -size);
    GL11.glVertex3f(size, size, -size);
    GL11.glVertex3f(-size, size, -size);
    GL11.glEnd();

    // Reset OpenGL states
    GL11.glEnable(GL11.GL_DEPTH_TEST);
    GL11.glPopMatrix();
}
```

