To create a job with Quartz.NET to call an API every 8 hours, you need to follow these steps:

1. Create a new Console Application project in Visual Studio.

2. Install the Quartz.NET package. Right-click on your project > Manage NuGet Packages > Search for "Quartz" > Install the "Quartz" package.

3. Add the necessary using statements at the top of your program:

```csharp
using Quartz;
using Quartz.Impl;
using System;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
```

4. Create a new class called `ApiJob` that implements the `IJob` interface. This class will contain the logic to call your API. Add the following code:

```csharp
public class ApiJob : IJob
{
    public Task Execute(IJobExecutionContext context)
    {
        // TODO: Implement your API call logic here
        Console.WriteLine("Calling API...");

        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }
}
```

You can replace the `Console.WriteLine` line with your actual API call logic.

5. In your `Main` method, add the following code to schedule the job to run every 8 hours:

```csharp
public static async Task Main(string[] args)
{
    // Grab the Scheduler instance from the Factory
    var factory = new StdSchedulerFactory();
    var scheduler = await factory.GetScheduler();

    // Start the scheduler
    await scheduler.Start();

    // Define the job and tie it to our ApiJob class
    var job = JobBuilder.Create<ApiJob>()
        .WithIdentity("apiJob", "group1")
        .Build();

    // Trigger the job to run every 8 hours
    var trigger = TriggerBuilder.Create()
        .WithIdentity("trigger1", "group1")
        .StartNow()
        .WithSimpleSchedule(x => x
            .WithIntervalInHours(8)
            .RepeatForever())
        .Build();

    // Tell Quartz.NET to schedule the job using our trigger
    await scheduler.ScheduleJob(job, trigger);

    // Wait indefinitely to keep the console application running
    await Task.Delay(-1);
}
```

6. Run the console application. It will start the scheduler and schedule the job to run every 8 hours. The `ApiJob` class's `Execute` method will be called at the specified interval, and you can add your API call logic there.

