To find the second instance of a character in a string using indexOf(), you can utilize the fromIndex parameter to start the search after the first occurrence.

Here's an example:

```java
String str = "Hello, World!";
char target = 'o';

// Finding the first occurrence of the character
int firstIndex = str.indexOf(target);

// Finding the second occurrence of the character
int secondIndex = str.indexOf(target, firstIndex + 1);

System.out.println(secondIndex); 
```

In this example, we first find the index of the first occurrence of the character 'o' using indexOf(). Then, we use the second indexOf() method with the fromIndex parameter as `firstIndex + 1` to start the search after the first occurrence. The returned value will be the index of the second occurrence of the character in the string.

