To get the `idToken` of a service account for a Firebase project in Node.js, you can use the `google-auth-library` package. Here's an example of how to do it:

1. Install the required packages:

```shell
npm install google-auth-library
```

2. Create a JavaScript file (`getToken.js`, for example) with the following code:

```javascript
const {JWT} = require('google-auth-library');
const fs = require('fs');

// Path to your service account key JSON file
const keyPath = '/path/to/service-account-key.json';

// The Firebase project ID
const projectId = 'your-project-id';

// Read the service account key file
const keyFile = fs.readFileSync(keyPath, 'utf8');
const key = JSON.parse(keyFile);

// Create a new JWT client
const client = new JWT({
  email: key.client_email,
  key: key.private_key,
  scopes: ['https://www.googleapis.com/auth/firebase'],
});

// Get the ID token
client.authorize((err, tokens) => {
  if (err) {
    console.error('Error occurred while authenticating:', err);
    return;
  }

  console.log('ID token:', tokens.id_token);
});
```

Replace `/path/to/service-account-key.json` with the path to your service account key JSON file obtained from the Firebase Console. Also, replace `'your-project-id'` with the ID of your Firebase project.

3. Run the script:

```shell
node getToken.js
```

You should see the ID token printed in the console. Make sure you have the right permissions set up for the service account in your Firebase project.

Note: An `idToken` is associated with a user rather than a service account. If you want to authenticate as a service account, you should use an `accessToken` instead.

